    "text": "Clear All",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/?ea735457_page=3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC)Customer Acquisition Cost, or CAC, measures how much an organization spends to acquire new customers. See why it's so important to growth.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-acquisition-cost"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer Advisory BoardWhat is a Customer Advisory Board and how can you create and leverage one? Start learning the basics and benefits of CABs for product teams.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-advisory-board"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer DevelopmentWhat is Customer Development? Define and learn the 4 steps involved in the customer development process as well as its benefits and pitfalls.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-development"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer EmpathyCustomer empathy is understanding the underlying needs and feelings of customers. Learn how to put customer empathy into practice.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-empathy"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer ExperienceWhat is customer experience? Learn why it is so important and how to build a great customer experience strategy for your team.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-experience"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer FeedbackCustomer feedback is information from those who buy and use your product. Moreover, product managers, designers, marketers, and salespeople, depend on customer feedback to understand how to improve their product and messaging to succeed in the marketplace.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-feedback"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer Journey MapWhat is a Customer Journey Map? Discover how a customer journey map can illustrate how customers interact with your business.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/customer-journey-map"
  },
  {
    "text": "Customer ValidationCustomer validation is an essential phase of the product development process (i.e., the steps needed to take a product from concept to market availability.) It tests assumptions and hypotheses about the customer problem, target market, and product.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/what-is-customer-validation"
  },
  {
    "text": "DACI Decision-Making FrameworkWhat is the DACI Decision-Making Framework model and how can you use it to make collaborative decisions? Learn more about DACI Decision-Making Framework decision making in our overview..",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/daci"
  },
  {
    "text": "Daily ScrumWhat is a Daily Scrum? Daily scrums are quick meetings held each day for the members of the product development team working on a sprint.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/daily-scrum"
  },
  {
    "text": "Data Product ManagerA data product manager focuses on collecting, organizing, storing, and sharing product management data within an organization.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/data-product-manager"
  },
  {
    "text": "DEEP BacklogWhat is a DEEP Backlog? Learn more about what DEEP backlog means and other agile terminology in our agile product management glossary.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/deep-backlog"
  },
  {
    "text": "Definition of DoneIn the Scrum agile framework, the Definition of Done describes the list of requirements that the team agrees must be met to consider a user story or other backlog item complete. The specific criteria will vary by team, but a typical agile team\u2019s checklist for Definition of Done would include:",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/definition-of-done"
  },
  {
    "text": "Definition of ReadyDefinition of Ready describes the requirements that must be met in order for a story to move from the backlog to development.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/definition-of-ready"
  },
  {
    "text": "DependencyWhat is a project management Dependency? Learn more about Dependency mapping and other PM terminology in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/dependency"
  },
  {
    "text": "Dependency ManagementWhat is Dependency Management? Learn more about Dependency Management and other product terminology in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/dependency-management"
  },
  {
    "text": "Design ConceptThe definition of a design concept is a short description of the idea behind a planned product. We\u2019ll cover how to create one with your team.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/design-concept"
  },
  {
    "text": "Design OpsWhat is design ops, and why should you adapt it for your culture? Learn the basics of design ops and how to incorporate it into your team.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/design-ops"
  },
  {
    "text": "Design ThinkingDesign thinking is an innovative framework based on seeing problems or needs from users' perspectives. It requires thoroughly understanding your customers.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/design-thinking"
  },
  {
    "text": "DevOpsDevOps is a natural extension of the Agile ethos\u2014smaller, quicker development cycles that leverage feedback to influence future development.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/devops"
  },
  {
    "text": "Digital Product ManagerA product manager is responsible for driving the development of products to market success. A digital product manager holds this responsibility for digital products. These include software tools, apps, or any product developed and used electronically.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/digital-product-manager"
  },
  {
    "text": "Digital TransformationDigital transformation refers to the trend where businesses use digital technologies to enhance and replace existing business processes.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/digital-transformation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Disciplined Agile (DA)A broad overview of the disciplined agile framework for product development. Indcludes strengths and weaknesses as well as who should use DA.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/disciplined-agile"
  },
  {
    "text": "Disruptive InnovationDisruptive innovation is a term coined by Clayton M. Christensen to describe any type of innovation that creates a new industry, market, or business model which eventually \"disrupts\" an existing one.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/disruptive-innovation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Distinctive CompetenceDistinctive competence refers to a superior characteristic, strength, or quality that distinguishes a company from its competitors.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/distinctive-competence"
  },
  {
    "text": "DocumentationExplore how to document a product roadmap to help align your product team to meet their OKRs and develop a clear go-to-market plan.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/documentation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Dual-Track AgileDual-track agile is where the cross-functional product team breaks its daily development work into two tracks: discovery and delivery.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/dual-track-agile"
  },
